# Bug: the release build fails where the interpreter and the dev build
# succeed. This is the ray tracer cut down by deleting declarations while
# the failure held; it would not reduce further by whole declarations, and
# a 90-line model of the same shape did not fail.
#
#   kanso run main.kso --interp -- x        prints a 16x9 PPM, exit 0
#   kanso build main.kso && ./main x        the same bytes, exit 0
#   kanso build main.kso --release && ./main x
#     prints a few rows, then
#     error[runtime]: no overload of `-` matches these arguments
#
# What the failure needs, each found by removing it and watching the
# release build start working:
#   - `surface hemisphere` in tracer/render.kso, an arm that never runs for
#     the argument "x", whose ray takes its direction straight from a
#     generator record: `ray d.value rec.p`. Writing `d.value + vec/zero`
#     there makes the release build correct; `d.value * 1.0` does not.
#   - the mode reaching `tracer/run` through cli/cli.kso's `pick`, so that
#     it can be either marker. Passing `tracer/full_shading` straight from
#     here makes it correct.
import "./cli"
import "std/os"

os/args .> cli/main
